📊 Semmelweis Analysis System
A professional Django-based data analysis web application for managing and visualizing yearly and monthly clinic records.
The project demonstrates:


Full CRUD operations


Data visualization using Chart.js


CSV file upload and processing


Service-layer architecture


Clean UI design using Tailwind CSS


Separation of concerns (Models, Views, Forms, Services)



📁 Project Screenshots
All screenshots are located in the assets/ folder.

🏠 Dashboard
Main landing page of the system.


➕ Add Record Page
Used to create new yearly records.


🗂 Yearly Records List
Displays all yearly records in a structured table with:


Year


Clinic


Births


Deaths


Proportion of deaths


Edit & Delete actions




📊 Monthly Records Page
Displays monthly analysis with chart visualization.


📤 CSV Upload Page
Allows users to upload CSV files for bulk data import.
The system:


Receives the file


Processes it using Pandas


Saves data to the database


Automatically updates charts




🔐 Admin Panel
Django admin interface for managing database records.


🏗 System Architecture
The project follows Django best practices:
✔ Models
Define database structure.
✔ Forms
Handle validation and user input.
✔ Views
Control application logic.
✔ Services
Handle CSV processing and business logic.
✔ Templates
Render UI using inheritance.
✔ Static Files
Include charts and styling.

📈 Data Visualization
The system uses Chart.js to:


Compare clinics yearly


Display death proportions


Show monthly trends


Update dynamically after data changes



